    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The researchers conducted a groundwater data survey of managers and stakeholders across the state of California to learn more  about  their  current  groundwater  data  collection, use  and  sharing  practices,  and  to  identify  some  of  the common data-related issues that local agencies may face during  SGMA  implementation.  The  survey  responses indicate  that effective groundwater management is hindered by a range of data-related challenges.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Moran, Tara, Cravens, Amanda, Martinez, Janet and Szeptycki, Leon. (2016). Fulfilling the Promise of California’s Sustainable Groundwater Management Act: Improving Groundwater Data Collection and Understanding. Stanford Digital Repository.  Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/sg971rf0870",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "“From the Ground Down: Understanding the Local Groundwater Data Collection, Adequacy, and Sharing Practices  in  California,”  released  by  Water  in  the  West, a joint program of the Stanford Woods Institute for the Environment and the Bill Lane Center for the American West. T. Moran, A. Cravens, J. Martinez, and L. Szeptycki.",
            "type": "citation/reference",
